{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1355187-dragontongue-who-speaks-it","id":1355187,"title":"Dragontongue - Who Speaks It?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted","Dragon-Blooded"],"posts":[{"date":"2019-12-16T08:10:53-08:00","id":1355187,"title":"Dragontongue - Who Speaks It?","content":"Odd question, but...<br /> <br /> Who actually learns and speaks Dragontongue? It is described as a language &quot;of poets and princes&quot; and that in the satrapies there is a rush of poets and savants to learn Dragontongue. <br /> <br /> But.. Who actually speaks it? Do all the Great House scions learn it? Is it used in the halls of government? Is it more of a cultural tongue used by posh poets and in literature? Is it expected to be used by anyone in particular?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1807-serpent-axis","name":"Serpent Axis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1807_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"135"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-16T08:48:46-08:00","id":1355193,"title":"","content":"I have a Character that speaks it <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> Solar Dawn Monk of the Cult of the Illuminated.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\">The problem with defending the purity of the English language is that English is about as pure as a cribhouse whore. We don't just borrow words; on occasion, English has pursued other languages down alleyways to beat them unconscious and rifle their pockets for new vocabulary. - James. D. Nicoll</span></span></i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/540-tymeaus-jalynsfein","name":"Tymeaus Jalynsfein","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"869"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-16T09:24:38-08:00","id":1355197,"title":"","content":"NPCs.<br /> <br /> It's a silly idea invented to explain why more Dynasts don't know Old Realm. Thus the intended use is pretty much 'any educated person in the Realm' honestly though, Exalted already has enough languages so I've yet to use it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4086-croakamancer","name":"Croakamancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4086_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"490"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-16T13:45:12-08:00","id":1355256,"title":"","content":"In past editions... Dragon-Kings.<br /> <br /> I know there's new fluff now. I'm ignoring it. It's dumb.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-16T14:15:14-08:00","id":1355266,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JohnDoe244</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1355187-dragontongue-who-speaks-it?p=1355256#post1355256\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In past editions... Dragon-Kings.<br /> <br /> I know there's new fluff now. I'm ignoring it. It's dumb.</div> </div> </div> </div>High Holy Speech was never called Dragontongue in past editions, so that's not true.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-16T15:32:44-08:00","id":1355282,"title":"","content":"Yeah, it was High Holy Speech for DKs.<br /> <br /> I don't really see the point of Dragontongue, since High Realm is already a fancy posh language. But my impression is it's a form of conspicuous consumption: you learn a fancy poetic language to prove how cultured you are, even though it has little practical use. Like how English public schools* teach students Latin and ancient Greek so Bojo can make himself sound clever quoting Virgil.<br /> <br /> *This is what Americans would call a private Prep school.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-16T16:02:54-08:00","id":1355285,"title":"","content":"I find Dragontongue makes a good deal of sense as an invention of Mnemon when it's interfaced with the expanded characteristics of House Mnemon itself. Something for all of those lofty dreamers to experiment and site off with.<br /> <br /> It's unusual, but has some novelty and invokes some of the less overused parts of Tolkien for those that are into it and is harmless otherwise. I'd say it also depends a bit on how much depth one wants to give the Linguistics Ability in terms of things like concepts that are more readily or artfully expressed in one language than another.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Croakamancer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1355187-dragontongue-who-speaks-it?p=1355197#post1355197\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Exalted already has enough languages</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm suddenly remembering that one but in Pinky and the Brain where they meet with a virtually uncontacted Island tribe and Brain starts making a rudimentary attempt at communication, only for the guy to cheerfully greet him and ask if he disks English in a comical Australian accent.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-16T19:26:31-08:00","id":1355321,"title":"","content":"In &quot;my&quot; Creation, I had Dragontongue be the <i>lingua franca</i> of the East during the Shogunate, the Greek to High Realm's Latin. After the River Province got turbofucked during the Great Contagion, Dragontongue basically died out, replaced by the tribal and regional languages of the peoples that migrated into the largely-depopulated East.<br /> <br /> Memnon &quot;rediscovered&quot; it, and it became <i>en vogue </i>for various high-class snoots and their hangers-on to learn it, sorta like how you learn Latin and Greek at a snob-fancy prep school......or how real-world Romans used Greek.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11892-boston123","name":"Boston123","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"790"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-16T21:38:28-08:00","id":1355337,"title":"","content":"I'd make it the language of the nobles of a region of the Blessed Isle. Kinda like a Breton to High Realm's French. Perhaps starting to form a seperate identity to the rest of the Isle that could become a full secessionist movement should the right people (Mnemon) not gain the throne","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1047-vampire-hunter-d","name":"vampire hunter D","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1047_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1727"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-17T00:51:55-08:00","id":1355346,"title":"","content":"In the Realm-based dragonblooded school game I'm in now only one of the PCs speaks Dragontongue and NPCs have actively suggested ignoring it. It doesn't really have a decent place, high realm already covers the high-society stuff and it really isn't a substitute for Old realm if you are a scholar. So unless you want to go heavily into poetry it is in an awkward place.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9124-satoshi","name":"satoshi","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"282"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-17T04:09:38-08:00","id":1355362,"title":"","content":"I'd play up the priestly language aspect. The purpose of Dragontongue is to give mortal worshipers a ceremonial language, much like reading a Catholic mass in Latin, that <i>doesn't </i>let them communicate with <i>random </i>spirits, read proscribed texts, or encounter dangerous phrases and concepts coded into the very parlance of Old Realm. It is mainly the language of missionaries and converts.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":487,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/487-greyman","user":"Greyman","date":". 12-17-2019, 07:18 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/487-greyman","name":"Greyman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar487_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1308"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-17T07:46:06-08:00","id":1355396,"title":"","content":"I use it as the language of Immaculate scripts.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>The Book of Laughing Serpents Series(Latest <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/293793/Book-of-Laughing-Serpents-Volume-7\" target=\"_blank\">Here</a>)<br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/287741/Many-Limbed-Manual?src=hottest_filtered&amp;filters=45622\" target=\"_blank\">Many Limbed Manual</a><br /> Patreon here: <a href=\"https://patreon.com/undeadauthorsociety\" target=\"_blank\">https://patreon.com/undeadauthorsociety</a><br /> San Jeanro Co-Op writer. Volume 1 <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/278871/The-Short-Games-Digest-Volume-1\" target=\"_blank\">here</a> Volume 2 <a href=\"https://t.co/SXRLElZlw4?amp=1\" target=\"_blank\">here</a> Volume 3 <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/297692/The-Short-Games-Digest-Volume-3?affiliate_id=389642\" target=\"_blank\">here</a><br /> My folklore and horror blog, here:<a href=\"http://undeadauthorsociety.wordpres.com/\" target=\"_blank\">http://undeadauthorsociety.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11835-epee102","name":"Epee102","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11835_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2102"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-17T15:48:20-08:00","id":1355505,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1355187-dragontongue-who-speaks-it?p=1355266#post1355266\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> High Holy Speech was never called Dragontongue in past editions, so that's not true.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ten characters.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lords of Creation, Page 29</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Dragontongue: The first artificial language, created centuries ago by the Dragon Kings as a way of establishing social dominance over the humans who served as their slaves at the time. The Dragon Kings themselves call this language \u201cHigh Holy Speech.\u201d</div> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-17T16:52:48-08:00","id":1355511,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JohnDoe244</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1355187-dragontongue-who-speaks-it?p=1355505#post1355505\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ten characters.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Huh. And here I thought that I had a full grasp of all of the bad ideas in DotFA.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-18T01:28:06-08:00","id":1355600,"title":"","content":"Well that's something new I learned. I don't think anywhere else called it an artificial language.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-18T03:47:24-08:00","id":1355607,"title":"","content":"You both might also want to revise the other appearances of the Tongue of the Dragon Kings (as it's referred to in Ruins of Rathes).<br /> <br /> Because. Yeah.<br /> <br /> It's described pretty much exactly as the new Dragontongue is (a constructed language derrived from Old Realm)... everywhere. Like literally everywhere the origins of the language is mentioned.<br /> <br /> The new Dragontongue vaguely alludes to High Holy Speech (&quot;elements of a priestly language that was lost&quot;). But I stand by what I said, the new fluff is for a language that doesn't have a niche. Realm commoners speak Low Realm, the rulers speak High Realm, the priests speak Old Realm. Dragontongue as the lost language of the Dragon Kings, used by poets, lost tribes and the more eccentric occultists, makes sense. Dragontongue as a dumbed down version of Old Realm which is somehow more difficult to write and thus only used by poets... is super niche. I'd allow it as a tribal language if a player really wanted it.<br /> <br /> <s>(Also, uh, didn't Holden write that bit of Lords and that bit of 3E? I'm pretty sure it's not accidental.)</s>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":531,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","user":"JohnDoe244","date":". 12-18-2019, 09:58 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-18T04:38:44-08:00","id":1355612,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JohnDoe244</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1355187-dragontongue-who-speaks-it?p=1355607#post1355607\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">(Also, uh, didn't Holden write that bit of Lords and that bit of 3E? I'm pretty sure it's not accidental.)</div> </div> </div> </div>Holden didn't join the gameline until years after DotFA first came out. He's credited in the revised version of Lords of Creation because he helped revise the high essence Solar charms.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-19T11:15:34-08:00","id":1355898,"title":"","content":"It <i>might</i> have a place if what it did was to neuter Old Realm in a New Speak sort of way. If someone could use Dragontongue in place of Old Realm for most practical uses but the strictures of grammar, conjugation, and definitions made certain ideas hard to express. For example, if it parsed Old Realm's &quot;Solar Exalted&quot; into something closer to &quot;One with the Sun's power&quot; it could avoid the implication that Celestials and Terrestrials properly belong to the same proper class.<br /> <br /> So &quot;native&quot; Dragontongue speakers who read an authentic Old Realm text or talk to a spirit who speaks it would require a fair bit more mental gymnastics and circumlocutions to understand the potentially dangerous or subversive content.<br /> <br /> While that might be an overexaggerated take on Sapier-Worf, the constructed languages of Exalted already have thaumaturgical and worshipful qualities built into their structure.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1144-exthalion","name":"Exthalion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1144_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2306"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-19T11:52:24-08:00","id":1355904,"title":"","content":"I treat Dragontongue as a beautiful written language and a guttural sounding one used by thieves and poets for different reasons. It is a convenient way to speak when you don't want most people to overhear you or understand. It is useful for code, but also can be used to convey ideas very poetically and visually pleasing way. Which makes nice art as well to the uneducated. but that is just my take.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4390-deamonlight","name":"Deamonlight","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"71"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-19T12:43:09-08:00","id":1355918,"title":"","content":"See I like both of those ideas from a world-building point of view.<br /> <br /> I see no reason why my PCs would spend merit dots on them. &quot;Would you like to spend 3XP on a language that makes it harder for you to understand things? How about cockney rhyming slang?&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-19T12:49:17-08:00","id":1355919,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JohnDoe244</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1355187-dragontongue-who-speaks-it?p=1355918#post1355918\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">See I like both of those ideas from a world-building point of view.<br /> <br /> I see no reason why my PCs would spend merit dots on them. &quot;Would you like to spend 3XP on a language that makes it harder for you to understand things? How about cockney rhyming slang?&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>Verisimilitude? Even the Lore 5, Occult 5 Twilight generally doesn't know the startup prayers for thousand forged dragons. You have to explain where you learned what you know. If every school in the Realm's sphere of influences teaches Dragontongue instead of Old Realm and it becomes the lingua franca among savants who interact with the Realm (since they will have the highest volume of occult publications, historical immaculate texts, etc) then most PCs should have it instead of Old Realm which there would be little opportunity for them to know.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1144-exthalion","name":"Exthalion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1144_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2306"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-19T12:59:21-08:00","id":1355924,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Exthalion</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1355187-dragontongue-who-speaks-it?p=1355919#post1355919\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Verisimilitude? Even the Lore 5, Occult 5 Twilight generally doesn't know the startup prayers for thousand forged dragons. You have to explain where you learned what you know. If every school in the Realm's sphere of influences teaches Dragontongue instead of Old Realm and it becomes the lingua franca among savants who interact with the Realm (since they will have the highest volume of occult publications, historical immaculate texts, etc) then most PCs should have it instead of Old Realm which there would be little opportunity for them to know.</div> </div> </div> </div>Firstly, does the Realm teach it instead of Old Realm?<br /> <br /> Secondly, why wouldn't my Supa-Special PC have learned Old Realm from her patron god? Or other been educated outside of proscriptive Realm schooling?<br /> <br /> Dragon-tongue needs to offer an advantage that makes it attractive to PCs. Not a punishment option for not Sueing your backstory.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-19T13:21:51-08:00","id":1355928,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JohnDoe244</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1355187-dragontongue-who-speaks-it?p=1355924#post1355924\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Firstly, does the Realm teach it instead of Old Realm?<br /> <br /> Secondly, why wouldn't my Supa-Special PC have learned Old Realm from her patron god? Or other been educated outside of proscriptive Realm schooling?<br /> <br /> Dragon-tongue needs to offer an advantage that makes it attractive to PCs. Not a punishment option for not Sueing your backstory.</div> </div> </div> </div>A: It doesn't work as I suggested in my original post RAW, it was a suggestion. If it did, then the suggestion that the Realm would teach it in preference to Old Realm would be a reasonable world-building step. Right now it is Memnon's Esparonto really only learned by people who want to suck up to her.<br /> <br /> B: Your super special PC could also be the son of Sol by M-r-l who was lost in the Wyld at the moment of your birth due to a cruel Yozi plot who has only just returned to restore your father's dream for a righteous Creation who can lean on that 5 dot mentorship to get appointed Shogun of Creation with all the proper paperwork filed such that all the gods obey you. People could also Sue themselves as the Solar Daughter of Memnon who's Exaltation convinced her mother to renounce the Immaculate Faith. At some point, you have to trust players to make characters that are interesting people that make sense as part of the world rather than torturous congeries of optimized dots.<br /> <br /> However, there would, at the very least, be the social benefit that would allow you access to the Realm+Inner Threshold world of scholarship without looking like a barbarian or an infernalist. Spirits in Immaculate territories might have learned to speak it and do so when interacting with people while refusing to acknowledge communications in Old Realm.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1144,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1144-exthalion","user":"Exthalion","date":". 12-19-2019, 04:33 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1144-exthalion","name":"Exthalion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1144_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2306"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-19T14:08:02-08:00","id":1355940,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JohnDoe244</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1355187-dragontongue-who-speaks-it?p=1355918#post1355918\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">See I like both of those ideas from a world-building point of view.<br /> <br /> I see no reason why my PCs would spend merit dots on them. &quot;Would you like to spend 3XP on a language that makes it harder for you to understand things? How about cockney rhyming slang?&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Sometimes it is nice to learn an obscure and hard language so others can't understand you. Even better if the language looks like art. Some people like to be pompus and learn for that reason alone. For a min-maxer? Language is a bunk merit, get the stone of the spoken word or whatever that translates for you.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4390-deamonlight","name":"Deamonlight","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"71"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}